    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15601" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρτεμίσιος</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρταμίτιος</span></b> , ὁ (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήν</span>), a Spartan and
		Macedonian month, <i><span class="en">
			Th.
			5.19
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Plu.
			<u>Alex.</u>
			16
		</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρτεμισιών</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶνος</span>, ὁ, at Erythrae, <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			410.1
		</span></i>
		<span class="entity">(iii B. C.)</span>, etc. [The first <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ι</span>
		in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀρτεμίσιον, -ίσιος, -ισιών,</span>
		etc., is long (cf. <i><span class="en">
			Ar.
			<u>Th.</u>
			1200
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Diph.
			124
		</span></i>) and written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ει</span> in Inscrr. of late
			<span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			12(9).234.23
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			708.1
		</span></i>, etc.]</div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
